{
  "about": "The roofs fixture's photo: synthetic 0.1 m source pixels (no swisstopo data) on the national 0.1 m grid, only the windows around the selected buildings' roofs, one file per 1 km tile the area touches (photo_<tile>.u8: the tile's windows' bytes one after the other, each window rows north to south, columns west to east, RGB interleaved, uint8). A window's west edge is E = west_dm / 10 m, its north edge N = north_dm / 10 m; its pixel (row j, column i) has its centre at E = west_dm / 10 + 0.05 + 0.1 i, N = north_dm / 10 - 0.05 - 0.1 j. Colours: R = 20 + i and G = 40 + j (counted inside each window), B = the building's number (12, 30, 48, ...: 12 + 18 x its place in chunk order) on the pixels whose centre lies in that building's roof by the rule, 0 elsewhere; on the roof of {8F14A0B6-0000-4000-8000-000000000016} R is 0 on 20 of its 40 pixel rows (the north and south rows among them) and 200 on the others, so its lower median is decided by one row. Windows: each selected building's footprint box grown by 2 pixels west, 5 east, 3 north, 7 south, clipped to the area box, merged where they overlap, cut at the 1 km tile edges.",
